{"v":1,"agent":"copilot-cli","cli_version":"0.10.6","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-09-23T10:42:59.639Z","id":"b2ab3218-73c9-4927-86f6-4385f1403cb7","content":[{"text":"The bug: the \"m c\" (mark-as-completed) and dispense proxy buttons in [encounter-details.tsx](src/pages/Encounters/tabs/overview/summary-panel-details-tab/encounter-details.tsx#L124-L129) used `className=\"hidden\"` (Tailwind `display: none`) purely to host their `ShortcutBadge`. But the shortcut resolver in [keyboardShortcutUtils.ts](src/Utils/keyboardShortcutUtils.ts#L69-L76) rejects any host whose `getClientRects().length === 0` — which is exactly what `display: none` elements return. So pressing `m` then `c` matched the shortcut, but `resolveBestHost` always came back `undefined` and `.click()` never fired.\n\nFixed by swapping `hidden` for `sr-only` (visually hidden, but keeps a 1px×1px box so it still counts as \"rendered\"), matching the codebase's existing convention for visually-hidden-but-functional elements.","type":"text"}]}
